1
00:01:30,566 --> 00:01:31,551
=Tigers Sniff the Rose=

2
00:01:31,551 --> 00:01:33,560
(Based on the novel of the same name by Yiren Kuikui)

3
00:01:35,260 --> 00:01:38,260
=Episode 7=

4
00:02:02,940 --> 00:02:05,420
(Zhang Renjing)

5
00:02:09,340 --> 00:02:11,980
(Yu Cheng'an, Zhang Renjing)

6
00:02:25,740 --> 00:02:29,380
(Yu Cheng'an, Zhang Renjing,
Xu Mianmian)

7
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:46,740
(Luling, Yu Cheng'an, Zhang Renjing)

8
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:55,060
(Luling, Yu Cheng'an, Zhang Renjing,
Xu Mianmian)

9
00:03:00,980 --> 00:03:04,220
(Luling, Yu Cheng'an, Zhang Renjing,
Xu Mianmian)

10
00:03:39,560 --> 00:03:41,330
The good times are almost here.

11
00:03:43,330 --> 00:03:43,970
What do you mean?

12
00:03:47,250 --> 00:03:48,000
In a few days,

13
00:03:48,720 --> 00:03:49,970
Sigui Garden in Jinchang Ward

14
00:03:50,330 --> 00:03:51,330
will host the Peony Festival.

15
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:52,810
Didn't you know?

16
00:04:03,090 --> 00:04:03,650
I know.

17
00:04:06,820 --> 00:04:11,620
(Five Days Before the Peony Festival)

18
00:04:12,020 --> 00:04:15,660
(Sigui Garden)

19
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:18,570
Sir,

20
00:04:19,570 --> 00:04:20,800
are you here to see the black peony?

21
00:04:21,600 --> 00:04:22,240
You're too early.

22
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,010
They won't bloom for a few more days.

23
00:04:25,240 --> 00:04:26,010
Thank you for letting me know.

24
00:04:53,620 --> 00:04:55,620
♪A rough-cut gem, held close to heart♪

25
00:04:56,855 --> 00:05:02,325
♪Lean bamboo bones, yet mountain-bold♪

26
00:05:02,691 --> 00:05:05,191
♪Books bear no blade♪

27
00:05:06,420 --> 00:05:11,050
♪Yet tens of thousands of scrolls
can pierce the sky♪

28
00:05:11,980 --> 00:05:14,047
♪My body is the furnace,
flames reach the clouds♪

29
00:05:14,048 --> 00:05:14,780
(Young Yan Shang)

30
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,770
Mother, there's a well hidden here!

31
00:05:17,040 --> 00:05:19,010
Didn't Brother say he was thirsty
from walking?

32
00:05:19,010 --> 00:05:21,720
♪Winds gather, then drift apart♪

33
00:05:21,720 --> 00:05:22,650
Come, Shang.

34
00:05:23,090 --> 00:05:24,090
I'll draw some water for you both.

35
00:05:27,130 --> 00:05:27,770
Here, have some.

36
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:28,600
Thank you, Mother.

37
00:05:28,820 --> 00:05:30,460
♪In all I do, I have no regrets♪
(Young Yan Dalang)

38
00:05:32,040 --> 00:05:32,530
Mother,

39
00:05:33,090 --> 00:05:34,720
when will the black peony bloom?

40
00:05:35,210 --> 00:05:36,480
(Xie Jinghui, Yan Shang's Mother)
We've come a little too early.

41
00:05:37,210 --> 00:05:38,890
But even without the famous flowers,

42
00:05:39,690 --> 00:05:40,330
just look around,

43
00:05:40,970 --> 00:05:43,400
the garden is so peaceful,
with clouds reflected in the water...

44
00:05:44,010 --> 00:05:45,040
It's beautiful all the same.

45
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:48,160
♪Who'll wait with me for the boat home?♪

46
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,400
Mother, look! A butterfly!

47
00:05:51,200 --> 00:05:53,360
♪By noon, the mist will lift♪

48
00:05:53,460 --> 00:05:55,760
♪Rivers will bend♪

49
00:05:56,160 --> 00:05:59,400
♪I'll take the open road
and journey home♪

50
00:06:00,630 --> 00:06:05,300
♪With rosy clouds,
I bid the moon goodnight♪

51
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,960
♪And trade my old robes for new♪

52
00:07:02,330 --> 00:07:03,480
Xu Mianmian.

53
00:07:05,330 --> 00:07:06,090
Luling.

54
00:07:07,840 --> 00:07:08,570
Luling...

55
00:07:12,800 --> 00:07:13,530
Greetings, sir.

56
00:07:16,240 --> 00:07:17,629
So early in the morning,

57
00:07:17,671 --> 00:07:21,181
and you're already strolling
through the garden?

58
00:07:21,890 --> 00:07:22,840
You certainly know how
to enjoy yourself.

59
00:07:23,530 --> 00:07:24,450
Something's troubling me.

60
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:26,010
I'm just wandering around.

61
00:07:30,720 --> 00:07:32,210
Since you're in no hurry,

62
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:35,480
would you care to play a game of Go
with me?

63
00:07:37,280 --> 00:07:37,920
I'd be happy to.

64
00:07:38,650 --> 00:07:40,240
But we have no Go board here,

65
00:07:40,480 --> 00:07:41,090
nor any stones.

66
00:07:42,690 --> 00:07:45,130
Let the mind be our board
and our thoughts the stones.

67
00:07:45,400 --> 00:07:47,210
Who needs physical pieces?

68
00:07:48,160 --> 00:07:50,360
Would you care to join me

69
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:52,360
for a game of Go without a board?

70
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,130
(He's here for me.)

71
00:07:58,920 --> 00:07:59,650
(Who is he?)

72
00:08:00,240 --> 00:08:01,160
(Why me?)

73
00:08:02,160 --> 00:08:02,570
In that case,

74
00:08:03,240 --> 00:08:04,450
I'd be honored.

75
00:08:05,010 --> 00:08:07,090
Upper 6-3, corner approach.

76
00:08:07,360 --> 00:08:08,770
Upper 8-3, pincer attack.

77
00:08:09,210 --> 00:08:10,650
Upper 7-4, diagonal move.

78
00:08:11,040 --> 00:08:11,530
Upper...

79
00:08:12,650 --> 00:08:13,570
8-4, attachment.

80
00:08:14,360 --> 00:08:17,970
So young, yet you play by the book.

81
00:08:19,450 --> 00:08:20,650
Upper 7-6, jump.

82
00:08:21,970 --> 00:08:23,720
Judging by your clothes,

83
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:26,330
you're preparing for the imperial exams.

84
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:29,600
I imagine you're hoping to pass
with flying colors.

85
00:08:29,920 --> 00:08:30,280
Am I right?

86
00:08:32,290 --> 00:08:33,570
Upper 4-2, jump.

87
00:08:34,640 --> 00:08:35,290
To tell you the truth, sir,

88
00:08:36,120 --> 00:08:36,880
I came to the capital

89
00:08:37,720 --> 00:08:38,760
not to seek fame or office.

90
00:08:41,360 --> 00:08:42,810
Upper 5-2, diagonal move.

91
00:08:43,090 --> 00:08:43,720
Then why?

92
00:08:44,360 --> 00:08:45,240
Upper 3-7.

93
00:08:46,090 --> 00:08:47,240
I came to right

94
00:08:47,840 --> 00:08:48,640
a terrible wrong.

95
00:08:49,600 --> 00:08:51,120
Upper 8-5, hane.

96
00:08:52,840 --> 00:08:53,480
Young man,

97
00:08:53,970 --> 00:08:54,810
do you realize

98
00:08:55,290 --> 00:08:56,360
that in Sheng'an,

99
00:08:56,930 --> 00:08:58,210
wolves are in power,

100
00:08:58,520 --> 00:08:59,570
and injustices are

101
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:02,410
far too many to count?

102
00:09:05,240 --> 00:09:06,210
Upper 6-5, peep.

103
00:09:06,720 --> 00:09:07,970
Then I'll right one if I can.

104
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:10,930
Well said.

105
00:09:11,480 --> 00:09:12,880
You know there's a tiger
on the mountain,

106
00:09:13,290 --> 00:09:15,240
yet you head straight toward it.

107
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:17,170
What courage!

108
00:09:18,640 --> 00:09:20,880
Upper 7-5, connect.

109
00:09:21,520 --> 00:09:22,290
Careful, sir.

110
00:09:23,330 --> 00:09:24,210
3-9.

111
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,810
That's an excellent move!

112
00:09:29,760 --> 00:09:31,810
Upper 3-2, net.

113
00:09:40,210 --> 00:09:41,330
Got you!

114
00:09:45,970 --> 00:09:46,810
Greetings, Chancellor Liu.

115
00:09:51,450 --> 00:09:52,640
My respects, Chancellor.

116
00:09:53,450 --> 00:09:54,480
Forgive my earlier discourtesy.

117
00:09:55,170 --> 00:09:56,360
I meant no disrespect.

118
00:09:57,690 --> 00:09:59,410
You two, honestly!

119
00:10:00,450 --> 00:10:02,360
Your timing couldn't be worse!

120
00:10:02,640 --> 00:10:05,290
The game was just getting interesting.

121
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:07,690
Never mind. Let's go.

122
00:10:13,810 --> 00:10:14,450
Young man,

123
00:10:15,570 --> 00:10:16,480
don't forget,

124
00:10:17,240 --> 00:10:18,720
you and I still have

125
00:10:19,120 --> 00:10:20,570
an unfinished game.

126
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:24,480
Yes.

127
00:10:55,640 --> 00:10:56,120
Scissors.

128
00:11:02,720 --> 00:11:03,840
What are you grinning about?

129
00:11:07,240 --> 00:11:08,360
Was I smiling?

130
00:11:08,810 --> 00:11:09,240
Scissors.

131
00:11:13,600 --> 00:11:14,810
Ever since you went out,

132
00:11:14,970 --> 00:11:16,290
you've been grinning to yourself.

133
00:11:17,930 --> 00:11:19,090
Did something good happen?

134
00:11:19,840 --> 00:11:20,760
Did you see your sweetheart?

135
00:11:22,210 --> 00:11:23,240
What sweetheart?

136
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,480
I don't have one!

137
00:11:26,330 --> 00:11:27,360
What do you like about Yan Shang?

138
00:11:28,640 --> 00:11:29,170
No!

139
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,520
I was thinking about Liu Wenji.

140
00:11:32,330 --> 00:11:33,520
Then what do you like about Liu Wenji?

141
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:38,240
I'm not even sure if it's love.

142
00:11:38,810 --> 00:11:41,640
I suppose love means always
wanting to see someone

143
00:11:42,330 --> 00:11:44,000
and never wanting to leave
when you're together.

144
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:48,170
How did you know exactly
what I was thinking?

145
00:11:49,600 --> 00:11:50,360
You like him.

146
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,520
But does he like you?

147
00:11:56,120 --> 00:11:56,600
I don't know.

148
00:11:57,330 --> 00:11:58,170
But I could ask him.

149
00:11:58,450 --> 00:11:58,880
Ask him?

150
00:11:59,360 --> 00:12:00,210
How would you do that?

151
00:12:01,970 --> 00:12:03,840
Liu Wenji invited me
to the Peony Festival.

152
00:12:04,210 --> 00:12:05,290
I could ask him then.

153
00:12:06,810 --> 00:12:07,290
But

154
00:12:07,970 --> 00:12:09,360
I haven't asked for your permission yet.

155
00:12:10,360 --> 00:12:11,930
If you say no, I won't go.

156
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,360
Go if you want to.

157
00:12:14,970 --> 00:12:16,690
I won't be the villain
who keeps two lovers apart.

158
00:12:17,880 --> 00:12:18,600
But

159
00:12:19,640 --> 00:12:20,360
you should know

160
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:23,090
life is already hard enough for women.

161
00:12:24,050 --> 00:12:25,970
Don't give your heart away too easily.

162
00:12:32,570 --> 00:12:33,720
Your Highness, you're teasing me.

163
00:12:35,840 --> 00:12:36,840
If the day ever comes

164
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:38,720
when my dear Chunhua gets married,

165
00:12:39,290 --> 00:12:42,090
I'll give you the grandest wedding
send-off.

166
00:12:43,210 --> 00:12:44,640
Every young woman in Sheng'an

167
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:45,970
will envy you.

168
00:12:50,760 --> 00:12:51,050
No!

169
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:52,480
I won't marry.

170
00:12:53,810 --> 00:12:54,840
I want to stay with you forever,
Your Highness.

171
00:12:55,600 --> 00:12:56,600
Don't be silly.

172
00:12:57,240 --> 00:12:57,930
How sappy!

173
00:13:04,570 --> 00:13:06,210
Your Highness, why have you
embroidered so many fish?

174
00:13:07,360 --> 00:13:08,120
What bad luck!

175
00:13:11,640 --> 00:13:12,810
This year's imperial exams

176
00:13:13,170 --> 00:13:14,120
are fast approaching.

177
00:13:14,840 --> 00:13:16,810
You must focus entirely on your studies.

178
00:13:17,690 --> 00:13:18,410
Class dismissed.

179
00:13:21,520 --> 00:13:22,930
Thank you, sir.

180
00:13:23,940 --> 00:13:29,180
(Upright Heart, Sincere Intent)

181
00:13:40,930 --> 00:13:41,330
Yan Shang.

182
00:13:44,360 --> 00:13:44,810
Yan Shang?

183
00:13:49,240 --> 00:13:50,720
What's got you so lost in thought?

184
00:13:53,210 --> 00:13:55,000
I've been thinking about
an unfinished game of Go.

185
00:13:55,880 --> 00:13:56,880
The imperial exams are almost here,

186
00:13:57,690 --> 00:13:58,880
and you still have time
to think about Go?

187
00:14:00,240 --> 00:14:02,050
This morning, at Sigui Garden
in Jinchang Ward,

188
00:14:02,330 --> 00:14:03,240
I happened to meet
an elderly gentleman.

189
00:14:03,840 --> 00:14:04,840
We played a game of Go.

190
00:14:05,600 --> 00:14:07,000
Later, I heard someone call him

191
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,210
Chancellor Liu.

192
00:14:08,640 --> 00:14:09,360
Chancellor Liu?

193
00:14:11,570 --> 00:14:12,690
What was he doing at Sigui Garden?

194
00:14:16,810 --> 00:14:18,410
Well, there's something
you two don't know.

195
00:14:22,810 --> 00:14:23,600
Sigui Garden

196
00:14:24,210 --> 00:14:26,000
was once the residence
of the late Chancellor Ma.

197
00:14:26,840 --> 00:14:28,720
Scholars often held
literary gatherings there.

198
00:14:28,880 --> 00:14:31,760
I hear Chancellor Liu often
attended them in his youth,

199
00:14:31,970 --> 00:14:33,170
reciting poetry
and discussing philosophy.

200
00:14:34,170 --> 00:14:35,330
But nowadays,

201
00:14:35,760 --> 00:14:37,480
the garden has changed hands
several times.

202
00:14:37,720 --> 00:14:38,570
The place remains,
but the people are gone.

203
00:14:39,930 --> 00:14:40,640
Perhaps

204
00:14:41,360 --> 00:14:42,720
Chancellor Liu was feeling nostalgic.

205
00:14:44,810 --> 00:14:45,240
Yan Shang.

206
00:14:46,240 --> 00:14:47,290
You really are lucky.

207
00:14:47,810 --> 00:14:49,360
You met someone so influential
just by taking a stroll.

208
00:14:51,000 --> 00:14:51,690
I see.

209
00:14:53,050 --> 00:14:53,360
Oh, by the way,

210
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,970
there's a rare black peony
in Sigui Garden.

211
00:14:57,410 --> 00:14:58,720
Every year during the Peony Festival,

212
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,090
people from all over
the capital flock there.

213
00:15:01,480 --> 00:15:02,600
After the Rebellion
of the Seven Garrisons,

214
00:15:02,840 --> 00:15:05,050
nearly all the capital's famous temples
and gardens were destroyed.

215
00:15:05,330 --> 00:15:08,450
But the black peony at Sigui Garden
miraculously survived.

216
00:15:09,000 --> 00:15:10,840
That's why the festival
has grown so popular.

217
00:15:11,240 --> 00:15:12,570
Nobles gather there every year.

218
00:15:12,880 --> 00:15:13,520
Even...

219
00:15:19,050 --> 00:15:21,120
Even Grand Princess Luling

220
00:15:21,480 --> 00:15:22,760
attends in person every year.

221
00:15:23,570 --> 00:15:24,000
I hear

222
00:15:24,360 --> 00:15:27,290
she even has her own private pavilion
in the garden.

223
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:29,640
Someone like Grand Princess Luling

224
00:15:30,090 --> 00:15:30,880
also enjoys flowers too?

225
00:15:31,640 --> 00:15:32,330
Wei Shu,

226
00:15:32,690 --> 00:15:34,050
she's certainly not there
for the flowers.

227
00:15:34,810 --> 00:15:36,210
Haven't you two heard?

228
00:15:39,810 --> 00:15:40,930
The Grand Princess

229
00:15:41,360 --> 00:15:42,930
often uses festivals as an excuse

230
00:15:43,290 --> 00:15:44,290
to choose new male favorites

231
00:15:45,360 --> 00:15:46,450
and have secret rendezvous.

232
00:15:49,090 --> 00:15:50,240
She's a Grand Princess.

233
00:15:51,050 --> 00:15:52,290
Doing such things in secret,

234
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,450
isn't she afraid of putting herself
in danger?

235
00:15:55,000 --> 00:15:56,640
She takes guards everywhere she goes.

236
00:15:57,170 --> 00:15:59,000
She's surrounded by attendants
inside and out.

237
00:15:59,600 --> 00:16:00,170
Besides,

238
00:16:00,410 --> 00:16:01,480
who in Sheng'an

239
00:16:01,970 --> 00:16:03,240
would dare lay a finger on her?

240
00:16:04,760 --> 00:16:06,170
Last year, some fool

241
00:16:06,570 --> 00:16:07,699
barged into her private pavilion

242
00:16:07,741 --> 00:16:08,711
to present his writings to her.

243
00:16:09,290 --> 00:16:11,360
Unfortunately, he was hideously ugly.

244
00:16:11,450 --> 00:16:12,290
A real eyesore.

245
00:16:12,640 --> 00:16:14,410
The Grand Princess was furious.

246
00:16:14,640 --> 00:16:16,120
She immediately had her guards
drag him out

247
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:17,290
and beat him to death.

248
00:16:18,760 --> 00:16:20,210
A man's life was taken just like that,

249
00:16:20,840 --> 00:16:21,880
and no one dared question it.

250
00:16:23,520 --> 00:16:24,840
At this year's festival,

251
00:16:25,120 --> 00:16:26,429
I wonder how many

252
00:16:26,471 --> 00:16:28,469
handsome young men she'll choose

253
00:16:28,511 --> 00:16:29,671
to become her male favorites.

254
00:16:30,120 --> 00:16:30,570
Feng Xianyu,

255
00:16:30,970 --> 00:16:32,360
how did it go with your writings
yesterday?

256
00:16:34,720 --> 00:16:35,240
I...

257
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:36,840
Yesterday, I...

258
00:16:37,360 --> 00:16:37,840
Mr. Zhao.

259
00:16:39,720 --> 00:16:40,810
Writings, Writings!

260
00:16:41,170 --> 00:16:42,840
At least you have decent writing
to show.

261
00:16:43,090 --> 00:16:43,570
But me?

262
00:16:43,930 --> 00:16:45,360
My essays are complete rubbish!

263
00:16:45,570 --> 00:16:47,290
My father would break my legs
if he had to read another one!

264
00:16:48,930 --> 00:16:50,120
You're being too modest, Zhao.

265
00:16:50,570 --> 00:16:51,480
(Zhao, Student at the Imperial Academy)
Just look at me!

266
00:16:51,970 --> 00:16:52,480
Do I

267
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:53,930
look like I'm being modest?

268
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:56,640
If my father hadn't forced me,

269
00:16:56,970 --> 00:16:58,840
(Upright Heart, Sincere Intent)
I'd never have set foot in this academy!

270
00:16:59,520 --> 00:17:00,840
He gained admission through
family privilege

271
00:17:01,570 --> 00:17:02,600
and had his elders looking out
for him.

272
00:17:04,130 --> 00:17:05,610
What more could he ask for?

273
00:17:08,650 --> 00:17:09,890
(Peony Festival...)

274
00:17:10,690 --> 00:17:12,280
(The Grand Princess attends
every year...)

275
00:17:13,320 --> 00:17:14,210
(Private Pavilion...)

276
00:17:19,040 --> 00:17:19,410
Mr. Zhao!

277
00:17:20,800 --> 00:17:21,240
(Upright Heart, Sincere Intent)
Mr. Zhao!

278
00:17:22,850 --> 00:17:23,800
Mr. Zhao, wait!

279
00:17:24,720 --> 00:17:25,080
What is it?

280
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,280
Could we speak in private?

281
00:17:33,040 --> 00:17:33,320
Come on.

282
00:17:36,130 --> 00:17:36,890
What do you want?

283
00:17:37,130 --> 00:17:38,170
Why all the secrecy?

284
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,760
A man of your standing, Mr. Zhao,

285
00:17:41,210 --> 00:17:43,240
shouldn't have to worry
about a few essays.

286
00:17:45,210 --> 00:17:45,720
Unlike me.

287
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:47,410
Apart from writing,

288
00:17:47,610 --> 00:17:48,610
I have nothing to offer.

289
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,480
If you're interested, Mr. Zhao,

290
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:55,000
I could provide you with a few essays

291
00:17:55,610 --> 00:17:56,760
to present to potential patrons.

292
00:17:58,170 --> 00:17:59,170
You'd do that for me?

293
00:18:02,930 --> 00:18:04,480
You're not giving them away for free,
are you?

294
00:18:07,040 --> 00:18:08,480
Nothing gets past you, Mr. Zhao.

295
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,210
I've been rather

296
00:18:10,970 --> 00:18:11,760
short on money lately.

297
00:18:12,320 --> 00:18:13,410
As for the cost of writing materials,

298
00:18:13,930 --> 00:18:14,690
I wonder if you'd be willing

299
00:18:15,410 --> 00:18:16,320
to cover my expenses?

300
00:18:18,970 --> 00:18:19,800
Then we have a deal!

301
00:18:22,480 --> 00:18:23,210
Well... Didn't see that coming.

302
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:25,320
Our teacher's always
praising your talent.

303
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:27,450
Who knew you'd be practical enough
to do something like this?

304
00:18:28,890 --> 00:18:29,720
Even a gentleman needs money.

305
00:18:30,130 --> 00:18:31,080
Nothing to be ashamed of.

306
00:18:33,280 --> 00:18:33,650
So tell me,

307
00:18:34,520 --> 00:18:34,930
how much?

308
00:18:40,760 --> 00:18:41,560
That much?

309
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:43,170
I could buy myself a top courtesan
for that!

310
00:18:44,850 --> 00:18:46,480
It might be expensive for others,

311
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:48,000
but for someone like you,

312
00:18:48,520 --> 00:18:49,800
it's just the cost of a few banquets.

313
00:18:55,320 --> 00:18:55,720
Fine.

314
00:18:56,240 --> 00:18:56,800
I'll pay.

315
00:18:57,690 --> 00:18:58,480
But let's get one thing straight.

316
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,280
Those essays had better be good!

317
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,080
And write plenty of them!

318
00:19:01,280 --> 00:19:02,000
Rest assured, Mr. Zhao.

319
00:19:03,080 --> 00:19:03,520
Thank you.

320
00:19:04,130 --> 00:19:04,520
I'll be off.

321
00:19:07,040 --> 00:19:07,610
It's a deal.

322
00:19:10,620 --> 00:19:15,460
(Two Days Before the Peony Festival)

323
00:19:15,930 --> 00:19:16,240
Sir.

324
00:19:17,760 --> 00:19:18,210
Young man.

325
00:19:18,850 --> 00:19:19,480
(Sigui Garden)
We meet again.

326
00:19:20,320 --> 00:19:21,240
You certainly are eager.

327
00:19:21,610 --> 00:19:23,650
The black peony won't bloom
for another two days.

328
00:19:24,930 --> 00:19:26,210
I have nothing else to do,

329
00:19:26,720 --> 00:19:28,320
so I thought I'd enjoy the garden
while it's quiet.

330
00:19:30,130 --> 00:19:30,410
By the way,

331
00:19:31,080 --> 00:19:31,760
I've heard

332
00:19:31,850 --> 00:19:34,040
Grand Princess Luling
has a private pavilion in the garden.

333
00:19:34,320 --> 00:19:35,800
Which one is it?

334
00:19:36,240 --> 00:19:37,930
Whenever the Grand Princess
comes to see the flowers,

335
00:19:38,040 --> 00:19:39,720
she takes over Jifang Pavilion.

336
00:19:44,410 --> 00:19:45,040
To tell you the truth, sir,

337
00:19:45,610 --> 00:19:47,240
I haven't found anyone willing
to back me lately.

338
00:19:47,690 --> 00:19:48,690
When the Grand Princess arrives,

339
00:19:49,280 --> 00:19:50,170
might I request an audience?

340
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,370
Sir,

341
00:19:51,800 --> 00:19:52,520
you mustn't.

342
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:55,450
The Grand Princess forbids anyone
from disturbing her during her visits.

343
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,520
Last year, a young man knocked
on her door seeking an audience.

344
00:19:57,800 --> 00:19:58,800
She wouldn't even open the door.

345
00:19:58,890 --> 00:20:01,130
Her guards came out
and beat him half to death!

346
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:06,040
Thank you for the warning, sir.

347
00:20:22,170 --> 00:20:22,560
Wenji.

348
00:20:24,450 --> 00:20:24,850
Wenji.

349
00:20:27,690 --> 00:20:28,240
You're back.

350
00:20:30,370 --> 00:20:32,320
An old servant just delivered a chest.

351
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:33,850
He said

352
00:20:34,280 --> 00:20:36,520
his master was surnamed... Zhao.

353
00:20:47,650 --> 00:20:47,970
Shang.

354
00:20:48,970 --> 00:20:49,760
These money...

355
00:20:51,560 --> 00:20:53,080
I wrote some essays for him.

356
00:20:53,170 --> 00:20:54,720
This is my payment.

357
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,000
You...

358
00:20:58,800 --> 00:20:59,690
Are you short on money?

359
00:21:00,370 --> 00:21:01,370
Why didn't you tell me?

360
00:21:01,480 --> 00:21:02,320
I could've lent you some!

361
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:06,520
We're friends. There's no need
to talk about loans.

362
00:21:07,480 --> 00:21:08,040
I'm not short of money.

363
00:21:08,320 --> 00:21:08,890
I just need more of it.

364
00:21:09,370 --> 00:21:10,170
Living in the capital is expensive.

365
00:21:10,610 --> 00:21:11,760
You should save your money too.

366
00:21:15,560 --> 00:21:16,930
If I'm not mistaken,

367
00:21:17,970 --> 00:21:19,650
you had a lovestruck look on your face
just now.

368
00:21:22,850 --> 00:21:23,720
I asked Chunhua

369
00:21:24,650 --> 00:21:26,970
to go to the Peony Festival
with me in two days.

370
00:21:28,850 --> 00:21:31,040
So you've got two happy occasions
coming up!

371
00:21:32,970 --> 00:21:33,690
Congratulations!

372
00:21:35,040 --> 00:21:35,890
What two occasions?

373
00:21:37,800 --> 00:21:38,690
Passing the imperial exams

374
00:21:39,040 --> 00:21:39,890
and getting married.

375
00:21:40,320 --> 00:21:41,480
What could be better than that?

376
00:21:45,970 --> 00:21:46,370
Shang.

377
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,170
As for the imperial exams,

378
00:21:48,610 --> 00:21:50,410
I can study hard and earn my success.

379
00:21:51,170 --> 00:21:52,240
But marriage is another matter.

380
00:21:59,890 --> 00:22:01,240
Even if I truly wanted to marry her,

381
00:22:01,800 --> 00:22:02,280
I'm afraid

382
00:22:02,800 --> 00:22:04,040
my father would never approve.

383
00:22:05,080 --> 00:22:05,690
After all,

384
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,040
she's only a...

385
00:22:09,320 --> 00:22:09,650
She's...

386
00:22:14,850 --> 00:22:15,970
Whether you two end up together

387
00:22:16,650 --> 00:22:18,130
ultimately depends on what you want.

388
00:22:32,930 --> 00:22:34,170
It's too early to talk about that.

389
00:22:36,760 --> 00:22:37,690
I need to go out.

390
00:22:38,170 --> 00:22:39,370
Don't wait for me for dinner.

391
00:22:41,370 --> 00:22:41,760
Shang.

392
00:22:42,610 --> 00:22:43,450
Where are you going?

393
00:22:44,930 --> 00:22:47,210
To see what it's like
to spend a fortune.

394
00:22:54,170 --> 00:22:54,890
This money

395
00:22:55,480 --> 00:22:56,480
should be enough to buy your freedom.

396
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,040
I can't accept something for nothing.

397
00:23:05,170 --> 00:23:06,560
Please tell me what you want.

398
00:23:08,480 --> 00:23:08,890
It's nothing difficult.

399
00:23:09,760 --> 00:23:10,560
All I need is for you

400
00:23:11,040 --> 00:23:12,410
to do me one small favor.

401
00:23:16,410 --> 00:23:19,690
(Sharpening scissors!
Kitchen knives for sale!)

402
00:23:20,560 --> 00:23:22,189
(Get your scissors sharpened!)

403
00:23:22,231 --> 00:23:25,469
(Come take a look!
Beautiful patterned cloth!)

404
00:23:25,511 --> 00:23:25,881
Sir.

405
00:23:26,450 --> 00:23:27,610
Need your scissors sharpened?
Or want a kitchen knife?

406
00:23:33,720 --> 00:23:34,130
Sir,

407
00:23:34,850 --> 00:23:35,970
how much is this little knife?

408
00:23:36,450 --> 00:23:37,040
This one?

409
00:23:37,410 --> 00:23:37,970
Fifty.

410
00:23:41,280 --> 00:23:41,800
Young man,

411
00:23:42,170 --> 00:23:43,040
take a look at this one.

412
00:23:44,320 --> 00:23:45,280
Fine craftsmanship, quality steel.

413
00:23:45,690 --> 00:23:46,720
Only three hundred.

414
00:23:50,610 --> 00:23:51,040
No, thank you.

415
00:23:52,610 --> 00:23:53,130
Sir.

416
00:23:53,610 --> 00:23:54,800
I'll be straight with you.

417
00:23:55,690 --> 00:23:57,210
This knife may be cheap,

418
00:23:57,520 --> 00:23:58,720
but after just a few uses,

419
00:23:59,610 --> 00:24:00,760
the blade will probably go dull.

420
00:24:01,520 --> 00:24:02,130
When it comes to knives,

421
00:24:02,320 --> 00:24:03,450
it's worth paying more.

422
00:24:03,760 --> 00:24:04,610
It may cost a little extra,

423
00:24:04,890 --> 00:24:06,130
but it'll last you for years.

424
00:24:06,280 --> 00:24:06,930
Thank you, sir.

425
00:24:07,520 --> 00:24:08,210
Once will be enough.

426
00:24:09,080 --> 00:24:10,040
All right. Thank you!

427
00:24:11,930 --> 00:24:12,690
Take care.

428
00:24:15,210 --> 00:24:17,130
(Get your scissors sharpened!)

429
00:25:12,450 --> 00:25:13,320
Captain! It's me! It's me!

430
00:25:13,520 --> 00:25:13,970
It's me!

431
00:25:17,210 --> 00:25:18,560
So you're already awake, Captain.

432
00:25:19,280 --> 00:25:20,210
I was just wondering

433
00:25:20,410 --> 00:25:22,240
how hard I'd have to slap you
to wake you up.

434
00:25:24,370 --> 00:25:26,800
I've crawled out of piles of corpses.

435
00:25:27,610 --> 00:25:29,189
I never sleep that deeply.

436
00:25:29,231 --> 00:25:30,301
You think I need you to slap me awake?

437
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:31,410
Of course.

438
00:25:31,800 --> 00:25:32,690
What is it? Spit it out!

439
00:25:49,240 --> 00:25:50,389
Well, well!

440
00:25:50,431 --> 00:25:51,711
Her personal handkerchief.

441
00:25:52,850 --> 00:25:53,520
Smells lovely!

442
00:25:54,930 --> 00:25:56,800
Congratulations, Captain.
You've gotten your wish.

443
00:25:57,130 --> 00:26:00,650
That little minx actually said yes?

444
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:01,520
Rest assured, Captain.

445
00:26:02,170 --> 00:26:04,930
Xu Mianmian simply didn't appreciate
your sincere feelings before.

446
00:26:05,520 --> 00:26:06,690
Once I explained everything,

447
00:26:07,040 --> 00:26:08,080
she was filled with regret.

448
00:26:08,930 --> 00:26:10,560
That's why she asked me to deliver
this embroidered handkerchief

449
00:26:11,040 --> 00:26:12,130
as a token of her affection.

450
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:17,170
At least she knows what's good for her!

451
00:26:17,480 --> 00:26:19,280
Xu Mianmian also asked me to tell you

452
00:26:19,800 --> 00:26:22,480
that she'd like to meet you
at Sigui Garden in Jinchang Ward

453
00:26:22,930 --> 00:26:24,210
to satisfy her longing for you.

454
00:26:32,930 --> 00:26:33,760
But...

455
00:26:35,650 --> 00:26:37,560
if that little minx wants to be with me,

456
00:26:38,890 --> 00:26:40,480
why meet in a garden?

457
00:26:41,520 --> 00:26:42,610
There's something you should know,
Captain.

458
00:26:43,320 --> 00:26:44,720
In two days, Sigui Garden

459
00:26:45,320 --> 00:26:46,650
will host the Peony Festival.

460
00:26:47,040 --> 00:26:48,320
It's quite a spectacular event.

461
00:26:49,040 --> 00:26:52,210
The garden has secluded pavilions
hidden among the flowers and trees.

462
00:26:53,040 --> 00:26:54,130
A secret rendezvous there...

463
00:26:54,850 --> 00:26:55,370
Wouldn't that

464
00:26:56,410 --> 00:26:57,760
add a little excitement?

465
00:27:01,650 --> 00:27:03,800
You're getting me all worked up!

466
00:27:05,370 --> 00:27:06,690
You sly devil!

467
00:27:07,720 --> 00:27:09,720
You scholars have all sorts of tricks.

468
00:27:10,240 --> 00:27:10,890
You know how to have fun.

469
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:12,320
Good.

470
00:27:13,760 --> 00:27:14,080
Good.

471
00:27:14,760 --> 00:27:15,970
You've done a fine job!

472
00:27:16,720 --> 00:27:18,720
From now on, your recommendations,

473
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:19,800
your official career...

474
00:27:21,410 --> 00:27:21,890
Leave it all to me!

475
00:27:24,520 --> 00:27:26,720
It's my honor to be of service, Captain.

476
00:27:28,320 --> 00:27:28,690
Good!

477
00:29:16,420 --> 00:29:18,500
(One Day Before the Peony Festival)
(Bright Virtue)

478
00:29:18,560 --> 00:29:19,410
(Virtuous and Learned)
(You go ahead to the dining hall.)

479
00:29:19,760 --> 00:29:20,560
(I'm going back to my dormitory.)

480
00:29:20,800 --> 00:29:21,210
(All right.)

481
00:29:22,040 --> 00:29:22,429
(See you tomorrow.)

482
00:29:22,471 --> 00:29:23,119
(Thank you for your hard work, sir.)

483
00:29:23,161 --> 00:29:23,441
(All right.)

484
00:29:24,610 --> 00:29:25,080
(Let's go.)

485
00:29:26,080 --> 00:29:26,610
(Hurry to the dining hall.)

486
00:29:27,890 --> 00:29:28,240
(Wait for me.)

487
00:29:30,610 --> 00:29:31,040
Sir.

488
00:29:33,040 --> 00:29:34,800
I'd like to request a day off tomorrow.

489
00:29:36,690 --> 00:29:37,410
What for?

490
00:29:39,080 --> 00:29:40,040
I've heard

491
00:29:40,370 --> 00:29:42,450
there's a Peony Festival
in Jinchang Ward tomorrow.

492
00:29:42,930 --> 00:29:43,890
It's one of Sheng'an's grandest events.

493
00:29:44,560 --> 00:29:45,690
I'd really love to see it.

494
00:29:46,130 --> 00:29:46,970
I was hoping...

495
00:29:48,930 --> 00:29:49,480
I'd say

496
00:29:50,080 --> 00:29:51,450
you're not really interested
in the flowers.

497
00:29:52,970 --> 00:29:54,610
You're hoping to find
a powerful supporter, aren't you?

498
00:30:00,210 --> 00:30:00,560
Fair enough.

499
00:30:01,410 --> 00:30:02,720
The annual Peony Festival
is a fine opportunity

500
00:30:03,280 --> 00:30:05,560
for scholars like you to win
the influential officials' favor.

501
00:30:05,970 --> 00:30:06,280
Very well.

502
00:30:07,130 --> 00:30:07,480
You may go.

503
00:30:08,480 --> 00:30:09,210
Thank you, sir.

504
00:30:22,450 --> 00:30:23,450
When you left,

505
00:30:23,690 --> 00:30:25,080
the prince and I had just
gotten married.

506
00:30:25,890 --> 00:30:27,210
Now three years have passed,

507
00:30:27,760 --> 00:30:29,650
(Liang Lingyi, Princess Consort of Jin)
and I still haven't borne him a child.

508
00:30:31,410 --> 00:30:32,040
Wanyao,

509
00:30:32,650 --> 00:30:33,850
of everyone in Sheng'an,

510
00:30:34,410 --> 00:30:35,410
I think you're the only one

511
00:30:35,930 --> 00:30:37,320
who truly understands my suffering.

512
00:30:39,080 --> 00:30:39,800
I don't understand.

513
00:30:41,890 --> 00:30:42,170
But...

514
00:30:43,240 --> 00:30:45,370
You were married for three years
without having children too.

515
00:30:57,210 --> 00:30:59,760
I've never intended to bear children
for anyone.

516
00:31:01,480 --> 00:31:02,370
I'm afraid you've misunderstood me.

517
00:31:04,690 --> 00:31:06,410
Even if your husband is gone,

518
00:31:06,480 --> 00:31:07,800
you shouldn't say things like that.

519
00:31:08,320 --> 00:31:09,720
You're a princess of the Huai Dynasty.

520
00:31:10,370 --> 00:31:11,280
Remarrying would be easy for you.

521
00:31:12,520 --> 00:31:13,720
Besides, you're still young.

522
00:31:14,240 --> 00:31:16,280
Don't worry. You can still
have children.

523
00:31:20,610 --> 00:31:21,760
Then let's hope you're right.

524
00:31:25,320 --> 00:31:26,240
Have you heard?

525
00:31:26,890 --> 00:31:29,000
The Peony Goddess at Sigui Garden

526
00:31:29,210 --> 00:31:31,080
is said to grant prayers for children.

527
00:31:32,850 --> 00:31:33,320
Cailian.

528
00:31:34,080 --> 00:31:34,650
Put these away.

529
00:31:35,520 --> 00:31:35,890
Yes, Your Highness.

530
00:31:41,370 --> 00:31:43,000
The Peony Festival is tomorrow.

531
00:31:43,720 --> 00:31:44,800
Why not come with me?

532
00:31:45,210 --> 00:31:46,080
I'll pray for a child,

533
00:31:46,450 --> 00:31:48,080
and you can draw a fortune for love.

534
00:31:49,210 --> 00:31:50,210
Thank you for the kind invitation.

535
00:31:50,850 --> 00:31:53,130
The festival will be crowded.

536
00:31:54,210 --> 00:31:54,930
I'm not used to crowds.

537
00:32:05,760 --> 00:32:06,210
All right, then.

538
00:32:07,040 --> 00:32:08,320
You should think carefully

539
00:32:08,720 --> 00:32:10,560
about what a woman's life is really for.

540
00:32:11,130 --> 00:32:12,450
If you change your mind,

541
00:32:12,760 --> 00:32:13,760
send someone to the Prince of Jin's
residence

542
00:32:14,210 --> 00:32:15,240
to let me know.

543
00:32:15,690 --> 00:32:16,000
All right.

544
00:32:17,650 --> 00:32:18,450
Let me see you out.

545
00:32:18,850 --> 00:32:19,450
No need.

546
00:32:30,720 --> 00:32:32,040
Your Highness, Yang Si is here.

547
00:32:32,850 --> 00:32:33,800
What does he want this time?

548
00:32:38,170 --> 00:32:39,040
Did I say you could come in?

549
00:32:41,000 --> 00:32:41,760
How did you get in here?

550
00:32:41,930 --> 00:32:43,520
Well, nobody told me I couldn't.

551
00:32:43,970 --> 00:32:45,280
I know this residence
like the back of my hand.

552
00:32:45,650 --> 00:32:47,040
I could find my way to you
with my eyes closed.

553
00:32:48,480 --> 00:32:49,650
Well? What do you want?

554
00:32:51,080 --> 00:32:54,450
The Peony Festival at Sigui Garden
in Jinchang Ward is tomorrow.

555
00:32:56,370 --> 00:32:57,560
I... I'll take you.

556
00:32:58,040 --> 00:32:58,450
Not interested.

557
00:32:59,410 --> 00:33:00,210
Why not?

558
00:33:00,800 --> 00:33:02,170
If you're not going with me,
who else would you go with?

559
00:33:02,410 --> 00:33:03,410
That man named Wei Shu?

560
00:33:05,170 --> 00:33:05,930
You're too late.

561
00:33:07,040 --> 00:33:08,450
I'm going with the Princess Consort
of Jin.

562
00:33:10,210 --> 00:33:11,560
What are you going with her for?

563
00:33:12,240 --> 00:33:13,080
To pray for a child.

564
00:33:44,080 --> 00:33:45,280
(Besides, you're still young.)

565
00:33:45,800 --> 00:33:46,450
(Don't worry.)

566
00:33:46,970 --> 00:33:48,040
(You can still have children.)

567
00:33:57,450 --> 00:33:57,760
Shang.

568
00:33:58,320 --> 00:33:58,850
How's my ironing?

569
00:33:59,320 --> 00:33:59,760
Is it smooth enough?

570
00:34:01,450 --> 00:34:01,850
Looks good.

571
00:34:03,080 --> 00:34:03,720
You're not even looking.

572
00:34:08,600 --> 00:34:08,970
Wenji.

573
00:34:10,410 --> 00:34:11,080
Get some rest.

574
00:34:11,600 --> 00:34:12,290
I'm going for a walk.

575
00:34:13,850 --> 00:34:14,410
At this hour?

576
00:34:14,890 --> 00:34:15,480
Aren't you going to bed?

577
00:34:15,770 --> 00:34:16,330
I can't sleep.

578
00:34:32,460 --> 00:34:36,900
(Auspicious Blessings Fill the Streets)

579
00:34:39,800 --> 00:34:43,560
(Fragrances Shop)

580
00:35:04,120 --> 00:35:04,520
Your Highness.

581
00:35:04,890 --> 00:35:05,560
It's time to rest.

582
00:35:09,640 --> 00:35:10,250
I can't sleep.

583
00:35:10,850 --> 00:35:11,480
You go get some rest.

584
00:35:13,160 --> 00:35:14,080
I'd like to stay up a little longer.

585
00:35:21,520 --> 00:35:22,200
If you don't leave,

586
00:35:22,930 --> 00:35:24,040
you'll have to drink with me.

587
00:35:27,850 --> 00:35:28,330
Your Highness,

588
00:35:29,640 --> 00:35:31,040
that day Shang came to the residence,

589
00:35:32,480 --> 00:35:33,480
I was the one who invited him.

590
00:35:34,080 --> 00:35:35,000
Why did you invite him?

591
00:35:36,040 --> 00:35:37,040
Were you trying to drive Yang Si mad?

592
00:35:37,970 --> 00:35:40,080
How was I supposed to know
he'd run into Yang Si?

593
00:35:40,560 --> 00:35:41,890
You've had trouble sleeping for years.

594
00:35:42,600 --> 00:35:44,250
The only time you slept well
was in Lingnan.

595
00:35:45,290 --> 00:35:45,850
So I thought

596
00:35:46,250 --> 00:35:47,770
perhaps it was because Shang was
with you.

597
00:35:48,250 --> 00:35:49,370
He's always been good with words.

598
00:35:50,600 --> 00:35:52,520
I thought if I invited Shang over

599
00:35:52,930 --> 00:35:54,640
to keep you company
like he did in Lingnan,

600
00:35:54,930 --> 00:35:56,000
perhaps you'd sleep better.

601
00:35:56,770 --> 00:35:57,770
You silly girl.

602
00:35:58,450 --> 00:35:59,890
Where do you get these ideas?

603
00:36:13,620 --> 00:36:15,900
(Princess Danyang's Residence)

604
00:36:17,940 --> 00:36:20,060
(Princess Danyang's Residence)

605
00:36:26,250 --> 00:36:27,250
What's he doing here?

606
00:36:29,970 --> 00:36:30,890
Yan Shang.

607
00:36:32,680 --> 00:36:33,450
I'll go bring him in.

608
00:36:51,250 --> 00:36:51,640
Your Highness.

609
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:00,410
In the middle of the night,

610
00:37:00,850 --> 00:37:02,410
lurking outside my residence...

611
00:37:03,640 --> 00:37:04,890
What mischief are you up to?

612
00:37:06,930 --> 00:37:07,730
I couldn't sleep tonight.

613
00:37:08,520 --> 00:37:09,970
So I decided to take a walk.

614
00:37:10,810 --> 00:37:12,600
I must've wandered farther
than I intended.

615
00:37:14,680 --> 00:37:15,520
So,

616
00:37:16,080 --> 00:37:17,160
you just happened

617
00:37:17,850 --> 00:37:18,810
to end up here?

618
00:37:20,250 --> 00:37:20,730
I suppose so.

619
00:37:22,250 --> 00:37:23,330
And why did you invite me inside,

620
00:37:24,770 --> 00:37:25,730
Your Highness?

621
00:37:32,330 --> 00:37:33,160
It's a long, dull night.

622
00:37:33,930 --> 00:37:34,970
I summoned you to tell me a story.

623
00:38:00,850 --> 00:38:02,160
What kind of story would you
like to hear, Your Highness?

624
00:38:04,640 --> 00:38:06,810
I thought you'd ask me why,

625
00:38:07,890 --> 00:38:09,040
or fly into a rage

626
00:38:09,680 --> 00:38:10,600
and storm off.

627
00:38:22,120 --> 00:38:22,560
Your Highness,

628
00:38:24,770 --> 00:38:25,600
it's cold at this hour.

629
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:28,080
Drinking could harm your health.

630
00:38:35,000 --> 00:38:36,040
Why are your hands so cold?

631
00:38:37,810 --> 00:38:38,730
Can't you afford warm clothes?

632
00:38:41,330 --> 00:38:42,080
I was in such a hurry to get here,

633
00:38:42,930 --> 00:38:43,930
I forgot to put on a cloak.

634
00:38:46,770 --> 00:38:47,850
Don't try to make me pity you.

635
00:38:48,640 --> 00:38:49,930
If your story is good,

636
00:38:51,200 --> 00:38:52,250
I'll give you that cloak

637
00:38:52,810 --> 00:38:53,890
as a reward.

638
00:38:56,450 --> 00:38:58,730
You certainly have plenty of cloaks,
Your Highness.

639
00:39:08,450 --> 00:39:09,160
Go on.

640
00:39:09,810 --> 00:39:10,520
Tell me

641
00:39:11,080 --> 00:39:11,930
whatever you wish.

642
00:39:20,120 --> 00:39:21,600
Then I'll tell Your Highness

643
00:39:22,520 --> 00:39:24,120
a story about a venomous snake
and a hornet.

644
00:39:28,890 --> 00:39:29,560
Once upon a time,

645
00:39:30,160 --> 00:39:31,160
there was a venomous snake.

646
00:39:32,000 --> 00:39:32,890
It was being chased by humans.

647
00:39:33,930 --> 00:39:35,370
At its most vulnerable moment,

648
00:39:36,080 --> 00:39:37,330
it encountered a hornet.

649
00:39:38,250 --> 00:39:39,850
One crawled on the ground,

650
00:39:40,080 --> 00:39:41,080
while the other flew through the air.

651
00:39:42,200 --> 00:39:43,520
Their paths should never have crossed.

652
00:39:44,410 --> 00:39:44,930
But unexpectedly,

653
00:39:46,080 --> 00:39:47,410
the hornet suddenly swooped down

654
00:39:47,890 --> 00:39:50,160
and stung the snake viciously
on the head.

655
00:39:51,810 --> 00:39:53,120
Did the snake die from the sting?

656
00:39:55,040 --> 00:39:55,410
No.

657
00:39:56,890 --> 00:39:58,120
Its fate was far worse.

658
00:39:59,370 --> 00:40:02,040
The hornet's venom remained
inside the snake's head.

659
00:40:02,930 --> 00:40:04,600
Day after day, year after year,

660
00:40:05,520 --> 00:40:07,640
it suffered constant, burning agony.

661
00:40:09,410 --> 00:40:09,890
And so,

662
00:40:11,080 --> 00:40:12,480
the pain lasted ten whole years.

663
00:40:14,160 --> 00:40:15,120
Unable to bear the pain,

664
00:40:16,200 --> 00:40:17,970
the snake searched everywhere
for the hornet.

665
00:40:18,810 --> 00:40:20,000
It searched for many years.

666
00:40:21,680 --> 00:40:23,200
But one crawled on the ground,

667
00:40:23,930 --> 00:40:25,000
while the other flew through the air.

668
00:40:25,890 --> 00:40:27,040
How could it ever find the hornet?

669
00:40:28,640 --> 00:40:29,120
And yet,

670
00:40:30,040 --> 00:40:30,930
fate had other plans.

671
00:40:31,560 --> 00:40:32,579
One day, the snake

672
00:40:32,621 --> 00:40:33,831
crossed paths with that same hornet.

673
00:40:34,640 --> 00:40:36,520
The very one that had stung its head.

674
00:40:38,330 --> 00:40:40,200
The snake invited the hornet
to travel with it.

675
00:40:41,330 --> 00:40:41,770
Sure enough,

676
00:40:42,520 --> 00:40:43,810
the hornet hadn't changed its ways

677
00:40:44,330 --> 00:40:45,200
and tried to sting the snake again.

678
00:40:46,410 --> 00:40:48,560
But this time, the snake didn't flee.

679
00:40:48,970 --> 00:40:50,850
Instead, it willingly offered
up its head.

680
00:40:55,000 --> 00:40:57,810
Just as the hornet plunged its stinger
into the snake's head,

681
00:40:59,560 --> 00:41:00,450
the snake thrust its head

682
00:41:01,480 --> 00:41:03,250
beneath the wheel of a passing carriage.

683
00:41:05,370 --> 00:41:07,000
The snake's head and the hornet

684
00:41:08,250 --> 00:41:09,450
were crushed beneath the wheel.

685
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:12,810
They were both dead.

686
00:41:15,120 --> 00:41:16,250
That was a terrible story.

687
00:41:17,520 --> 00:41:18,450
You're not getting that cloak.

688
00:41:19,160 --> 00:41:19,850
What was wrong with it?

689
00:41:24,040 --> 00:41:25,160
Even if the snake killed the hornet,

690
00:41:25,850 --> 00:41:27,000
it wouldn't cure the pain in its head.

691
00:41:28,160 --> 00:41:30,040
Such revenge would accomplish nothing.

692
00:41:30,890 --> 00:41:31,480
And worse still,

693
00:41:32,120 --> 00:41:33,080
they both ended up dead.

694
00:41:35,250 --> 00:41:36,680
There are countless ways
to kill a hornet

695
00:41:37,250 --> 00:41:38,200
and take revenge.

696
00:41:39,000 --> 00:41:40,770
Why sacrifice its own life to do it?

697
00:41:42,250 --> 00:41:43,160
Don't tell me

698
00:41:43,890 --> 00:41:44,640
such foolish stories again.

699
00:41:46,520 --> 00:41:47,730
You're absolutely right, Your Highness.

700
00:41:53,520 --> 00:41:54,600
(But if one day,)

701
00:41:55,330 --> 00:41:57,080
(I get the chance to kill my enemy
with my own hands,)

702
00:41:58,250 --> 00:42:00,290
(what does it matter if it's foolish?)

703
00:43:02,480 --> 00:43:02,970
Your Highness.

704
00:43:06,770 --> 00:43:07,410
I must leave.

705
00:44:03,500 --> 00:44:07,740
(Next Episode Preview)

706
00:44:09,450 --> 00:44:10,890
Seal off the entire garden!

707
00:44:11,000 --> 00:44:12,250
Until that filthy wretch is caught,

708
00:44:12,560 --> 00:44:13,600
no one is leaving!

709
00:44:14,080 --> 00:44:15,450
There's been a murder in the garden.

710
00:44:15,560 --> 00:44:18,000
Aunt! I heard someone
was killed in the garden!

711
00:44:18,330 --> 00:44:20,200
Aunt, I really can't stand
the sight of blood!

712
00:44:20,480 --> 00:44:21,520
Let her go! Let her go!

713
00:44:21,850 --> 00:44:22,520
You're the best!

714
00:44:24,481 --> 00:44:27,774
♪Be the ferry
where you wait for the sun♪

715
00:44:30,459 --> 00:44:35,375
♪Be the blue silk
that catches your tears♪

716
00:44:37,569 --> 00:44:43,414
♪Be the sleeve we held,
worn by dust and years♪

717
00:44:43,914 --> 00:44:49,140
♪Let's conspire to grow old together♪

718
00:44:51,909 --> 00:44:56,700
♪Let me be a captive beast
bound by the same lock as you♪

719
00:44:57,536 --> 00:45:03,615
♪- Through trails of mud and blood;
- let grief drown in your eyes♪

720
00:45:05,416 --> 00:45:08,566
♪Soar with the wind;
plunge into hellfire as one♪

721
00:45:08,566 --> 00:45:10,214
♪Burning bright as a song♪

722
00:45:10,266 --> 00:45:13,990
♪See how roses and green bamboo enchant♪

723
00:45:14,368 --> 00:45:19,034
♪Be the vow I make with all my heart♪

724
00:45:19,653 --> 00:45:23,694
♪If we say forever,
then forever it shall be♪

725
00:45:24,185 --> 00:45:26,300
♪Not a single hour less♪

726
00:45:26,340 --> 00:45:33,286
♪However deep the snow,
I'll wait if you're there♪

727
00:45:34,049 --> 00:45:37,502
♪We'll be gods above,
or wandering souls♪

728
00:45:37,682 --> 00:45:40,827
♪In heaven or the underworld,
you're all I need♪

729
00:45:41,266 --> 00:45:47,903
♪If we can stay, let's return
to the village of our first meeting♪

730
00:45:48,300 --> 00:45:50,338
♪- May time be free of fear;
- boats rock♪

731
00:45:50,338 --> 00:45:52,814
♪- May time be free of pain;
- lights fade, seasons turn♪

732
00:45:52,852 --> 00:45:55,321
♪You're the only one I need♪

733
00:45:55,525 --> 00:46:02,412
♪Sharp winds or fierce rain,
nothing can break us♪

734
00:46:02,724 --> 00:46:05,995
♪Be mine in this world;
be mine in this life♪

735
00:46:06,300 --> 00:46:09,473
♪My last untouched innocence♪

736
00:46:09,797 --> 00:46:13,223
♪If only we could return
to the village where we first met♪

737
00:46:13,456 --> 00:46:16,681
♪Stay by me; help me forget
the frozen dream of last night♪

738
00:46:17,012 --> 00:46:23,808
♪Fireflies glow, flowers kiss our lips;
just us, through dawn and dusk♪

739
00:46:24,177 --> 00:46:26,239
♪- May time be free of fear;
- boats rock♪

740
00:46:26,240 --> 00:46:28,743
♪- May time be free of pain;
- lights fade, seasons turn♪

741
00:46:28,790 --> 00:46:31,128
♪You're the only one I need♪

742
00:46:31,359 --> 00:46:38,194
♪By your side, through joy and pain,
is that eternity?♪

743
00:46:38,543 --> 00:46:40,161
♪Till fireworks flood the town♪

744
00:46:40,291 --> 00:46:42,087
♪Till the lake is still and clear♪

745
00:46:42,444 --> 00:46:45,461
♪You're the only one I need♪

746
00:46:45,501 --> 00:46:46,828
(No animals were harmed
or mistreated in production.)
